  {
   "id": "stack",
   "nav": "Card stack",
   "title": "How the stack moves now",
   "sub": "Everything that moves with the scroll is still moved by the browser (sticky, fixed); the script only decides what is shown, and now also sets one transform per card while it opens or closes.",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "cards",
     "cols": 2,
     "items": [
      {
       "title": "The strips",
       "html": "Collar (the gap above a card and the bottom corners of the one it covers), cap (outside a card's top corners) and veil (the bottom edge of a card coming up) are each one hole with the card's corners, its shadow the page colour. One shape, one edge: no seams at fractional pixels. The cap's hole is 1.5px inside the card's outline, so a card's soft corner is drawn over white, never over the card before."
      },
      {
       "title": "Wide card layout",
       "html": "<code>--card-t</code> = min(the room the old square left, 2 × padding + 12.5 title letters). The drawing's room is the rest of the card; the drawing a square of min(1.08 × room width, card height), at least 300, centred."
      },
      {
       "title": "The drawing follows the open part",
       "html": "The open part is the card's top h px. Room beside the text: min(1.08 × room width, h); under it: min(1.08 × width, 1.04 × (h − text)). Scale = room(h) / room(open), moved by (h − open) / 2. Shown from half open (<code>SET.artAt</code> 0.5)."
      },
      {
       "title": "Titles",
       "html": "In: 0.8s, out of a 0.22em blur, 18% rise, lines 0.07s apart, the arrive curve. Out: 0.3s into the blur, the leave curve. A closing card hides its title <code>SET.titleLead</code> (12% of the card) early."
      },
      {
       "title": "The pinned pill",
       "html": "A fixed copy of the pill (<code>.stack__pin</code>), shown on the way down from the moment the card is a pill until the next card's first title is 0.4 pill from its edge (at most 0.3 screen after the next card is up). Leaves in 0.5s (up and out); scrolled back, in 0.22s. Re-armed only when the page has been above that moment. With reduce motion it goes at once."
      },
      {
       "title": "Sections after the stack",
       "html": "Get <code>position: relative; z-index: 1</code> from the script (were relative only), so they are drawn over the last card outright."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "nav",
   "nav": "Navbar",
   "title": "The navbar on sideways phones",
   "sub": "Only under <code>--sideways</code> (narrower than 1024, shorter than 500, landscape).",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "cards",
     "cols": 2,
     "items": [
      {
       "title": "Follows the scroll",
       "html": "Offset = the scroll since it last turned, between 0 and its height, never more than the page is past the hero's bottom edge. Set as <code>translate</code> each scroll event (no transition)."
      },
      {
       "title": "Settles",
       "html": "140ms without a scroll event: if it is part way, a glide to away (if it was last moving away and the hero is far enough up) or back. 0.42s on the arrive curve, starting at the speed it had."
      },
